hadiths[22]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18025","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us from Hafsah from Rabab al-Dabbiyyah from Salman ibn Amir al-Dabbi that he said: When one of you breaks his fast, let him break it upon dates, and if he does not find, let him break it upon water, for water is purifying."
"18026","Hisham said: And Asim al-Ahwal narrated to me that Hafsah raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"18027","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Hisham, he said: Hafsah narrated to me from Salman ibn Amir, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: With the boy is his aqeeqah, so shed blood on his behalf and remove harm from him."
"18028","He said: And I heard him saying: Your charity upon the poor is charity, and upon the near kin relative is two: charity and joining of ties."
"18029","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from Ibn Awn from Hafsah bint Sirin from al-Rabab Umm al-Raih bint Sulay from Salman ibn Amir al-Dabbi that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity upon the poor is charity, and upon the kin is two: charity and joining of ties."
"18030","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Asim from Hafsah from al-Rabab Umm al-Raih bint Sulay from Salman ibn Amir al-Dabbi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you breaks his fast, let him break it upon dates, and if he does not find, let him break it upon water, for it is purifying. And he said: With the boy is his aqeeqah, so shed blood on his behalf and remove harm from him. And he said: Charity upon the poor is charity, and upon the kin is two: joining of ties and charity. Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Asim from Hafsah from al-Rabab Umm al-Raih bint Sulay from Salman ibn Amir al-Dabbi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you breaks his fast, let him break it upon dates, and if he does not find, let him break it upon water, for it is purifying."
"18031","Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us from Ibn Sirin from Salman ibn Amir al-Dabbi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: With the boy is an aqeeqah, shed blood on his behalf and remove harm from him."
"18032","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Asim narrated to us from Hafsah from al-Rabab from Salman ibn Amir al-Dabbi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you breaks his fast, let him break it upon dates, and if he does not find dates, let him break it upon water, for it is purifying for him."
"18033","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us from Hafsah bint Sirin from al-Rabab from Salman ibn Amir al-Dabbi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you breaks his fast, let him break it upon dates, and if he does not find, let him break it with water, for water is purifying."
"18034","And he said: With the boy is his aqeeqah, so shed blood on his behalf and remove harm from him."
"18035","And he said: Charity upon the poor is charity, and upon the kin is two: joining of ties and charity."
"18036","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Ibn Numayr both said: Hisham narrated to us, and Yazid said: Hisham informed us from Hafsah bint Sirin from Salman ibn Amir al-Dabbi that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Ibn Numayr said that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: With the boy is his aqeeqah, so shed blood on his behalf and remove harm from him."
"18037","Affan narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, he said: Ayyub and Habib and Yunus and Qatadah informed us from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Salman ibn Amir al-Dabbi that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the boy: His aqeeqah, so shed blood on his behalf and remove harm from him."
"18038","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Asim narrated to us from Hafsah from al-Rabab from Salman ibn Amir al-Dabbi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you breaks his fast, let him break it upon dates, and if he does not find dates, let him break it upon water, for it is purifying for him."
"18039","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us from Ayyub from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Salman ibn Amir, and Ayyub did not mention the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"18040","And Hisham from Muhammad from Salman raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: For the boy is his aqeeqah, so shed blood on his behalf and remove harm from him."
"18041","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Ayyub and Qatadah from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Salman ibn Amir al-Dabbi that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the boy: His aqeeqah, so shed blood on his behalf and remove harm from him."
"18042","Waki narrated to us, he said: Ibn Awn narrated to us from Hafsah bint Sirin from al-Rabab Umm al-Raih bint Sulay from Salman ibn Amir al-Dabbi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity upon the poor is charity, and it is upon the near kin two: joining of ties and charity."
"18043","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us from Hafsah from Salman ibn Amir al-Dabbi, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Charity upon the poor is charity, and charity upon the kin is two: charity and joining of ties."
"18044","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us from Ibn Awn and Said from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Salman ibn Amir from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: With the boy is his aqeeqah, so shed the blood on his behalf and remove the harm from him. He said: And Ibn Sirin used to say: If removing the harm is not shaving the head, then I do not know what it is."
"18045","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us from Ibn Sirin from Salman ibn Amir al-Dabbi that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: With the boy is his aqeeqah, so shed the blood on his behalf and remove the harm from him."
"18046","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Asim from Hafsah from Salman ibn Amir from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever finds dates, let him break his fast upon them, and if he does not find dates, let him break his fast upon water, for water is purifying."
